OL,3,AWoman deceived ex-partner that she had
OL,4,Agiven birth to his babies, judge rules
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman convinced her former partner
OL,7,Fshe had given birth to two children who
OL,8,Fmost likely did not exist in what a
OL,9,FHigh Court judge described as an
OL,10,F"extraordinary" and "elaborate campaign
OL,11,Fof deceit".
OL,13,FThe man, who has not been named but was
OL,14,Freferred to as John during the hearing,
OL,15,Fapplied to the Family Court after he
OL,16,Fwas told the woman had sold their two
OL,17,Fchildren for a combined #500.
OL,19,FThe case heard that the man received
OL,20,Fmessages and photos of the children and
OL,21,Fpaid the woman around #30,000 over the
OL,22,Fcourse of two years.
OL,23,APub: 03-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
